      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let \\( F \\) be the force in pounds and \\( L \\) be the length of the handle in inches. According to the problem, the force required varies inversely with the length of the handle. This relationship can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[ F = \\frac{k}{L} \\]\nwhere \\( k \\) is a constant.\n\nFirst, we need to determine the constant \\( k \\) using the given values. We know that when the length \\( L = 9 \\) inches, the force \\( F = 375 \\) pounds. Substituting these values into the equation, we get:\n\\[ 375 = \\frac{k}{9} \\]\nTo find \\( k \\), we multiply both sides of the equation by 9:\n\\[ k = 375 \\times 9 = 3375 \\]\n\nNow that we have the constant \\( k \\), we can use it to find the force required for a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches. We substitute \\( L = 15 \\) and \\( k = 3375 \\) into the equation:\n\\[ F = \\frac{3375}{15} \\]\nPerforming the division, we get:\n\\[ F = 225 \\]\n\nTherefore, the force required to loosen the bolt with a wrench of 15 inches is \\(\\boxed{225}\\) pounds.",
